WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.700
There's a lot of
anxiety in the country.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.500
And as a result, we're
not hearing each other.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.033
We're not talking to each other.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:12.467
We stick with like-minded
people and have lost our ability

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:16.800
to appreciate that someone's
life experience may

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.333
be very different than yours.

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:24.166
What I tried to do with this
series is to not judge people,

00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:28.834
but to encourage an
open, honest dialogue,

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:34.233
actually listen to each
other, be critical thinkers,

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.333
and be open minded.

00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:38.734
These are really
complicated topics

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:46.266
to unpack, white anxiety, gender
inequality, tech addiction.

00:00:46.266 --> 00:00:50.000
I don't think this series is
going to change the world,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.300
but I'm hoping it
will help people

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.467
see a different perspective.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.433
ANNOUNCER: "America Inside
Out," with Katie Couric,

00:00:56.433 --> 00:00:57.433
Wednesday, April 11th at
10:00 on National Geographic.

